{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>תורת</b> — Yefet said: This is said about Aaron. And Rabbi Yeshuah said: about Phinehas. And the correct view is that it is said about both of them and about their holy sons, for thus it is fitting for a high priest to be." "<b>הייתה בפיהו</b> — He does not accept a bribe." "<b>ועולה</b> — To show favoritism." "<b>בשלום</b> — With Israel." "<b>ומישור</b> — To perform My commandments."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved 'Rabbi Yeshuah' as the medieval commentator; the epithet is preserved as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:12.509950849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}